OL,3,GNEWSATwo more hotels housing asylum
OL,4,Aseekers to close
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo hotels in Sussex will no longer be
OL,7,Fused to house asylum seekers.
OL,9,FThe Imperial Hotel in Hove and the
OL,10,FRamada by Wyndham in Crawley "will now
OL,11,Fbe handed back to communities in the
OL,12,FSouth East", the government has said.
OL,14,FBoth hotels were given three month's
OL,15,Fformal notice and are expected to close
OL,16,Fin December.
OL,18,FThe Imperial and Ramada are among 52
OL,19,Fhotels housing asylum seekers that the
OL,20,Fgovernment has announced will close
OL,21,Fthis year, leaving roughly 140 still in
OL,22,Foperation.
OL,23,APub: 19-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
